From d35e85a388c6e89e438cde9818d664eabe7a28db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 21:21:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] nvk/rm: enumerate RM GPUs and fill in the physical device

With NVK_RM=1 in the environment, NVK asks librmclient for the GPUs RM
knows about before looking at DRM devices.  For each one it opens an RM
client, allocates NV01_DEVICE_0 and NV20_SUBDEVICE_0 and fills
nv_device_info from RM:

  - chipset from NV2080_CTRL_CMD_MC_GET_ARCH_INFO (0x1b2 on GB202),
  - classes from NV0080_CTRL_CMD_GPU_GET_CLASSLIST_V2 (highest 3D,
    compute, copy, GPFIFO and usermode class Mesa knows about; Volta or
    newer is required for doorbell submission),
  - PCI ids, bus location, marketing name,
  - VRAM size and usage from NV2080_CTRL_CMD_FB_GET_INFO_V2,
  - GPC/TPC counts from NV2080_CTRL_CMD_GR_GET_INFO_V2,
  - SM limits the same way nouveau computes them.

No BAR heap is advertised: CPU-mappable memory will be backed by system
pages.  Logical devices are not implemented yet.

---
 src/nouveau/vulkan/meson.build              |   2 +
 src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/nvkmd.c            |   8 +
 src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/rm/nvkmd_rm_dev.c  |  17 +
 src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/rm/nvkmd_rm_pdev.c | 478 ++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 505 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/rm/nvkmd_rm_dev.c
 create mode 100644 src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/rm/nvkmd_rm_pdev.c

